error[E1309]: `atomic_load` does not admit `Order.release`
 --> mem:///main.lu:4:31
  |
4 |         let a = p.atomic_load(Order.release)
  |                               ^^^^^^^^^^^^^ not admitted here
  |
  = note: a load has no release half: its orders are `Order.relaxed`, `Order.acquire` and
    `Order.seq_cst` ([conc.mm.atomic.raw.2])

error[E1309]: the failure order `Order.acquire` is stronger than the success order `Order.release`
 --> mem:///main.lu:5:51
  |
5 |         let b = p.atomic_cas(0, 1, Order.release, Order.acquire)
  |                                                   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^ not admitted here
  |
  = note: a failed compare-and-swap is a load, so its order is `Order.relaxed`, `Order.acquire` or
    `Order.seq_cst`, and no stronger than the success order's load half
    ([conc.mm.atomic.raw.2])

error[E1309]: `fence` does not admit `Order.relaxed`
 --> mem:///main.lu:6:15
  |
6 |         fence(Order.relaxed)
  |               ^^^^^^^^^^^^^ not admitted here
  |
  = note: a relaxed fence orders nothing: a fence is `Order.acquire`, `Order.release`,
    `Order.acq_rel` or `Order.seq_cst` ([conc.mm.fence])

error[E1309]: `Order` has no mark `sequential`
 --> mem:///main.lu:7:32
  |
7 |         p.atomic_swap(a, Order.sequential)
  |                                ^^^^^^^^^^ not one of the five marks
  |
  = note: an atomic operation's order is one of `Order.relaxed`, `Order.acquire`, `Order.release`,
    `Order.acq_rel` or `Order.seq_cst` ([conc.mm.atomic.order])
